# Context First

Before planning or implementing, read the relevant living docs. **Full destination matrix:** [DOC-OWNERSHIP.md](../../.specs/codebase/DOC-OWNERSHIP.md). **Skills/agents inventory:** [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md).

| Change type | Start here |
| ----- | ----- |
| General code | `CONVENTIONS.md`, `STRUCTURE.md` |
| Scanner modules | `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `CONCERNS.md`, `INTEGRATIONS.md` |
| Progress / milestones | `ROADMAP.md`, `.specs/features/` |
| Decisions / deferred | `STATE.md` |
| Tests / gates | `TESTING.md`, `quality-gates.mdc` |
| Exit codes / flags | `docs/cli-reference.md` |

## Living documentation

Significant changes (modules, domain types, CLI flags) must land in the DOC-OWNERSHIP destination — do not mirror the same table into multiple SoTs. Feature complete → ROADMAP per [roadmap-sync.md](../skills/vitals-common/references/roadmap-sync.md). Editing a living doc → its glob-scoped `*-sot.mdc` (or `docs-sot.mdc`).

